      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poeciliopsis_prolifica_blackstripe_livebearer_en/",
      "html": "<ul><li>Origin: bred (captive-bred)</li><li>Maximum length: males 2 cm, females 3.5 cm</li><li>Peaceful species</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poeciliopsis_prolifica_blackstripe_livebearer_en/",
      "html": "<p>This tiny species of livebearer originates from northwestern Mexico. In nature they are even found in brackish waters.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poeciliopsis_prolifica_blackstripe_livebearer_en/",
      "html": "<p>This minuscule fish fits perfectly for nano tanks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poeciliopsis_prolifica_blackstripe_livebearer_en/",
      "html": "<p>Regarding the water chemistry they are completely undemanding.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poeciliopsis_prolifica_blackstripe_livebearer_en/",
      "html": "<p>The whole day through the males are after the females or fight their harmless clashes. When doing this they swim in a typical head-down position and spread the gonopodium at a 90° angle from the body.</p><p>It is possible to keep this peaceful species in a community tank, but they do much better in a species tank.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poeciliopsis_prolifica_blackstripe_livebearer_en/",
      "html": "<p>The males reach a maximum length of 2 cm, the females of 3.5 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/poeciliopsis_prolifica_blackstripe_livebearer_en/",
      "html": "<p>It is very interesting that the young are not born at one time, but over a period of several days. So an observer could get the idea that the fish give birth every day. This is why the species got its name.</p>"
    }
  ],
